--TEST--
hovering a call of a method an `extend` block adds shows its signature on the extended type, a sentence naming the block that adds it, and then its `///` run — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`, `rule:tooling/doc-comment-attaches-to-the-next-declaration`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

use Core\Time\Date;
use Shop\BusinessDays;

extend Date as BusinessDays {
    /// Whether the shop is open on this day.
    public function isBusinessDay(): bool {
        return $this->day() != 19;
    }
}

echo Date::at(2026, 9, 17)->isBusi<|>nessDay() ? "open" : "closed";
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
Core\Time\Date::isBusinessDay(): bool
```

`Shop\BusinessDays` adds this method to `Core\Time\Date`.

Whether the shop is open on this day.
